# What check.sh must find at the sync commit in SKILL.md: each rule that
# breaks in a setup, with TLC's shortest path to it (the actions, after
# the initial state). Every rule not listed holds. A line goes only when
# the code it describes changed, with the reason in the same change.

# Finding 1. `residue restore ENTRY` lands while a remove run purges that
# trash entry. trash::restore trusts the listing's lock, so it moves the
# worktree back after the purge unlocked it and while `git worktree remove`
# runs; Git then deletes the worktree's Git directory by id, at its original
# path, and restore_trash forgets the purge's removal record and its refs.
# Replayed on the release binary, 2026-11-09 (SKILL.md, "Findings").
Trash no-faults NotDeletedOnceBack: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind TList TCheck TMove GExists GGitdir
Trash no-faults ReflogCommitsKept: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind TList TCheck TMove GExists GGitdir TDiscard TForget
Trash no-faults RestoreTellsTheTruth: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind TList TCheck TMove GExists GGitdir TDiscard TForget TReport
Trash faults NotDeletedOnceBack: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind TList TCheck TMove GExists GGitdir
Trash faults ReflogCommitsKept: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind TList TCheck TMove GExists GGitdir TDiscard TForget
Trash faults RestoreTellsTheTruth: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind TList TCheck TMove GExists GGitdir TDiscard TForget TReport

# Finding 2. A restore unlocks by the lock its listing saw, and Git's
# `worktree unlock` lifts any lock: one the user set after the listing goes
# too (trash::restore `was_locked`, removed.rs move_back `ours`).
Trash no-faults OnlyOwnLocksLifted: PRecheck PRecord TList PUnlock TCheck UserLocks TUnlock
Trash faults OnlyOwnLocksLifted: PRecheck PRecord TList PUnlock TCheck UserLocks TUnlock
Remove no-faults OnlyOwnLocksLifted: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord SList SDest SCopies UserEdits RVerify PBCheck PBUnlock UserLocks PBMove PBStuck RSettle SMoveBack SUnlock
Remove faults OnlyOwnLocksLifted: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify SList RUnlock Kill SDest SCopies SMoveBack UserLocks SUnlock
Remove orphan OnlyOwnLocksLifted: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify SList RUnlock Orphan SDest SCopies SMoveBack UserLocks SUnlock

# Finding 3. Git is killed part way through deleting the files (residue's
# 30-minute REMOVE_TIMEOUT, or another kill of Git alone) while the .git
# file survives: standing() counts the worktree whole, so the record is
# dropped, and without --trash put_back says "it is back in place", with
# files gone.
Remove faults RecordDroppedOnlyWhenWhole: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify RUnlock GFind GExists GStatus GTree GitTimeout RAfter PBCheck PBMove RSettle
Remove faults RestoreTellsTheTruth: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify RUnlock GFind GExists GStatus GTree GitTimeout RAfter PBCheck PBMove SList SDest SCopies SAfter SReport
Trash faults RecordDroppedOnlyWhenWhole: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind GExists GStatus GTree GitTimeout PAfter PRelock PSettle
Remove after RecordDroppedOnlyWhenWhole: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify RUnlock GFind GExists GStatus GTree GitTimeout RAfter PBCheck PBMove RSettle
Trash after RecordDroppedOnlyWhenWhole: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind GExists GStatus GTree GitTimeout PAfter PRelock PSettle

# Finding 4. residue alone is stopped while its `git worktree remove` runs,
# by a signal to its PID only: Git runs in residue's process group, and
# residue sets no handler, so the Git child keeps deleting. move_back's guard
# is the PID in the aside name (Leftover::running), which is residue's PID,
# not Git's, so `residue restore RECORD` moves the worktree back, and Git
# then deletes its Git directory by id. Replayed on the release binary,
# 2026-11-09 (SKILL.md, "Findings"); the ReflogCommitsKept path needs Git to
# be slower than restore's checks after the move, and live Git was faster.
Remove orphan NotDeletedOnceBack: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify RUnlock GFind Orphan SList SDest SCopies SMoveBack SMove GExists GGitdir
Remove orphan ReflogCommitsKept: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify RUnlock GFind Orphan SList SDest SCopies SMoveBack SMove GExists SAfter GGitdir
Remove orphan RestoreTellsTheTruth: RRecheck RMove RLock RRecord RVerify RUnlock GFind Orphan SList SDest SCopies SMoveBack SMove GExists GGitdir SAfter SReport

# Finding 5. A purge is stopped with its Git child part way through the
# delete (Ctrl-C), leaving the entry unlocked and part of its files gone.
# `residue restore ENTRY` after it: trash::restore moves it back, and
# restore_trash forgets the purge's record and reports it back with no
# note that part of it is gone, where removed.rs move_back always says so.
# Replayed on the release binary, 2026-11-09 (SKILL.md, "Findings").
Trash after RestoreTellsTheTruth: PRecheck PRecord PUnlock GFind GExists GStatus GTree Kill TList TCheck TMove TDiscard TForget TReport
